Playtest-priority items:
- **180° reversal:** pressing Left while heading Right is ignored; no death. Up then Down inside one tick: Down ignored (reads as reversal of the pending turn), snake survives.
- **Quick double turn:** Up+Left pressed within one tick are both honoured on consecutive steps (no lost key, no self-reversal). 
- **Pressing 3 keys inside one tick:** the queue holds 2; the third is silently dropped (Up,Left,Down → Down lost). Acceptable, only noticeable to very fast players.
- **Speed:** 120 ms/tick, constant. A simple bot with 1-step lookahead, pressing keys at real time, reached scores of 17 and 22 without missing turns, so the speed is controllable (I cannot judge human feel). It never speeds up, so a long run gets easy; not a defect for this brief.
- **Food on snake:** sampled every ~20 ms across ~80 s of play and 39 foods: never on the snake.
- **Page scroll:** arrow keys never scrolled the page (scrollY 0, page fits the window at every size tried).
- **Pause:** P pauses/resumes, snake frozen while paused (04-paused.png); window blur auto-pauses.
- **Window sizes:** 800x500 to 1920x1080 all fit without scroll; board scales down on small windows and the HUD/footer stay visible (09-viewport-*.png).

## Problems and friction
1. **[Defect, build] ~30 failed requests / console errors on every load.** The page asks for `assets/theme.css`, `assets/images/{snake-head,snake-body,snake-tail,title-logo,board-tile,food}.png`, `assets/audio/{start,eat,gameover,music}.{ogg,mp3,wav}`, none of which exist; the delivered files are `assets/img/{head_up,…,food,body,bg_a,wall,logo}.png` and `assets/audio/*.wav`. Result: game uses fallback drawing and, as far as I could see, plays with **no sound at all** (not heard: headless; but the audio files requested do not exist). This is the known "sprites not wired" gap, but it also breaks the brief's "no console errors" standard and the sound path. Fix: make `src/assets.js` and the `<link>` in `index.html` use the artist's real filenames (or the artist's `assets/manifest.json`).
2. **[Minor] Head vs body hard to tell at a glance** in the fallback drawing: head is a slightly lighter green square with two tiny dots. Readable when the snake is moving, weak when it is long (run 0 reached length 20). Sprites should fix this; re-check on the next build.
3. **[Minor] Death is abrupt:** the screen switches immediately to the Game Over overlay; a player pressing Enter/Space just as they die (rapid key mashing) could restart instantly without seeing the score. I did not hit it by accident, but there is no short delay.
4. **[Minor] Opening-state food:** the first food can appear directly in the snake's path 2–3 cells away; nothing unfair seen.

